---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { evidenceUrl, url } from "../lib/specs";
import budget from "../../../docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/budget.json";
import sources from "../../../docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/source-revisions.json";
const packed20 = budget.raw_and_snapshot_budgets.filter(row => row.bits_pair===20);
const usbBytes = budget.constants.usb_full_speed_wire_bits_s/8;
const raw80 = packed20.find(row => row.pairs_s===80000000)!;
const pinRows = [["SPIBone / config select","1","G3"],["SPIBone / config clock","2","F3"],["Bidirectional SPIBone / config data","3","F2"],["FPGA reset","4","G4"],["FPGA done","5","F4"],["FPGA status","6","A4"],["Oscillator enable","19","Enable input"]];
---
<Base title="FPGA routes and capacity gates">
<header class="page-title"><p class="eyebrow">ADIUVO FORGIX / PCIE CANDIDATE / S3 REFERENCE</p><h1>Put the FPGA where<br />the samples can reach it.</h1><p class="lede">The source review selects a bounded snapshot/SPI route. Forgix cannot drain raw 80 MS/s IQ over its full-speed USB connection. Physical revision, wiring and sustainable transport remain unverified.</p><p><a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/README.md")}>Reviewed inventory and limits</a> · <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/forgix-preservation/README.md")}>MCU preservation proof</a> · <a href={url("work/?work=the-fpga-route-has-a-measured-feasibility-decision")}>Open the feasibility proposal →</a></p></header>
<div class="card-grid"><article class="research-card"><p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY DESIGN / ACTUAL BOARD UNVERIFIED</p><h3>Adiuvo Forgix</h3><p>RP2354 and Efinix Trion T8F49, 7,384 logic elements, eight multipliers and 15 KiB FPGA block memory. The official design has 3.3 V I/O and USB full-speed at 12 Mb/s through the RP.</p><p>Reviewed PSRAM wiring terminates at RP QSPI. It is not a directly connected FPGA sample memory. The F49 package has no dedicated JTAG pins; start from the documented RP/passive-SPI configuration path.</p><p><strong>Candidate roles:</strong> counters, triggers, small FIFOs, bounded SPI snapshots and filtered lower-rate or spectral results.</p><a href="https://forgix.tech/">Official Forgix design ↗</a></article><article class="research-card"><p class="eyebrow">READ-ONLY HOST SURVEY / NO DMA PROOF</p><h3>PCIe FPGA candidate</h3><p>The dabc:1017 endpoint is unbound and disabled. Sysfs reports a current 8 GT/s ×4 link and maximum ×8. A 512 MiB BAR aperture is an address window, not a measured memory capacity.</p><p>Prior attributed notes associate it with Alibaba AS02MC04 / XCKU3P. Exact board markings, accessible GPIO, bank voltage, clocks, configuration storage and recovery remain physical gates.</p><p>No driver binding, BAR access, JTAG scan, bitstream programming or DMA benchmark was performed. The initial survey found no identifiable Forgix interface. Forgix now responds through its factory USB loader; MCU flash preservation and application return pass. FPGA transport remains untested.</p><a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/host-survey.json")}>Inspect the host survey →</a></article><article class="research-card"><p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY DEMONSTRATION / DIFFERENT CHIP</p><h3>eSpDR on ESP32-S3</h3><p>Dedicated S3 GPIO and SIMD feed an Artix-7 with DDR and FT600 USB 3. The original LX6 lacks that same demonstrated peripheral/instruction route.</p><p>Current upstream keeps the ESP crystal and forwards an ESP-generated clock to the FPGA. This is a separate architecture to investigate if continuous wideband capture becomes the priority.</p><a href="https://github.com/h0m3us3r/eSpDR/tree/41a0ffe279119df942e4a9e892dc19d196e1c952">Pinned reference design ↗</a></article></div>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">CALCULATED BOUNDS / NOT A BENCHMARK</p><h2>200 MB/s in. At most 1.5 MB/s out.</h2></div><p>80 MS/s × 20-bit packed IQ exceeds Forgix USB wire capacity by {Math.floor(raw80.packed_payload_bytes_s/usbBytes)}× before framing. A finite FIFO cannot repair that sustained mismatch.</p></div><div class="fact-strip"><div><small>RAW 80 MS/S / 20-BIT PAIRS</small><strong>{raw80.packed_payload_bytes_s/1e6} MB/s</strong><span>320 MB/s in 32-bit SRAM words</span></div><div><small>RP FULL-SPEED USB / WIRE BOUND</small><strong>{usbBytes/1e6} MB/s</strong><span>Application payload will be lower</span></div><div><small>ALL T8 BLOCK RAM / IDEAL FILL</small><strong>{(raw80.t8_all_memory_fill_seconds*1e6).toFixed(1)} µs</strong><span>Assumes all 15 KiB available</span></div><div><small>MAXIMUM SNAPSHOT / IDEAL DRAIN</small><strong>{raw80.minimum_usb_full_speed_drain_seconds*1000} ms</strong><span>40,950 bytes exceeds T8-only FIFO</span></div></div><div class="table-scroll measurement-table"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>Nominal acquisition</th><th>20-bit packed payload</th><th>32-bit SRAM words</th><th>Maximum original-chip window</th></tr></thead><tbody>{packed20.map(row => <tr><th scope="row">{row.pairs_s/1e6} MS/s</th><td>{row.packed_payload_bytes_s/1e6} MB/s</td><td>{row.sram_word_bytes_s/1e6} MB/s</td><td>{(row.maximum_snapshot_seconds*1e3).toFixed(5)} ms</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="calc-note">These calculations exclude headers, transaction gaps, CPU/DMA overhead and usable memory allocation. <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/budget.json")}>Open reproducible budget data ↗</a></p></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">CALCULATED / DECIMATION CANDIDATES</p><h2>Reduce data before asking USB to carry it.</h2></div><p>Anti-alias filtering must precede decimation. These rates assume every input sample exists; decimation cannot recover ESP capture gaps.</p></div><figure class="budget-chart"><svg viewBox="0 0 660 265" role="img" aria-labelledby="decimation-title"><title id="decimation-title">Calculated decimated payload versus 1.5 megabytes per second USB wire ceiling</title><line x1={140+1.5/12.5*365} y1="25" x2={140+1.5/12.5*365} y2="222" stroke="var(--unverified)" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />{Object.entries(budget.decimated_80msps_20bit_bytes_s).map(([factor,bytes],index) => <g><text x="10" y={55+index*47} fill="var(--ink)">÷{factor}</text><rect x="140" y={34+index*47} height="25" width={bytes/1e6/12.5*365} rx="3" fill={bytes>usbBytes ? "var(--unverified)" : "var(--accent)"} /><text x="525" y={52+index*47} fill="var(--ink-2)">{bytes/1e6} MB/s</text></g>)}<text x="140" y="248" fill="var(--muted)">Dashed line: USB wire ceiling; payload lower</text></svg><figcaption>Calculated from committed budget JSON. Factor 128 is still above the wire bound; factor 256 is only a candidate for a real throughput test.</figcaption></figure><div class="split"><article class="note-box"><h3>Small spectral results are another route</h3><p>Assumed 16-bit bins at ten frames per second cost {(budget.example_spectrum_bytes_s["256"]/1000).toFixed(2)} / {(budget.example_spectrum_bytes_s["1024"]/1000).toFixed(2)} / {(budget.example_spectrum_bytes_s["2048"]/1000).toFixed(2)} kB/s for 256 / 1,024 / 2,048 bins, before headers. This is a model for a control/spectrum role, not current firmware throughput.</p></article><article class="note-box"><h3>Bounded original-chip candidate</h3><p>Completed capture → validated copy/pack → ordinary ESP SPI DMA → FPGA FIFO/counter/trigger/decimator → RP SPIBone/USB. The reserved radio SRAM’s DMA reachability and real end-to-end capacity need physical tests.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">PINNED SOURCES / RESOLVE BEFORE WIRING</p><h2>The RP owns the existing config bus.</h2></div><p>Do not connect an ESP output to a signal the RP is already driving. The later data link needs verified spare edge I/O and defined signal ownership.</p></div><div class="table-scroll"><table class="lab-table"><thead><tr><th>Internal function</th><th>RP GPIO</th><th>FPGA ball / destination</th></tr></thead><tbody>{pinRows.map(row => <tr>{row.map((value,index) => index===0 ? <th scope="row">{value}</th> : <td>{value}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table></div><div class="split measurement-table"><article class="note-box"><h3>Revision and clock conflict</h3><p>The reviewed Adiuvo schematic identifies T8F49I2X, has a blank drawing revision and an oscillator part placeholder. The pinned LiteX platform selects T8F49C2 and assumes 32 MHz at B4. Verify actual FPGA grade and oscillator marking before compiling or selecting constraints.</p><p>ESP SPI3 documentation lists CS5/SCLK18/MISO19/MOSI23 for IO_MUX. Actual carrier access and voltages are unknown; that is a source mapping, not permission to attach guessed wires.</p></article><article class="note-box"><h3>First physical milestone</h3><p>Forgix factory USB identity and MCU preservation are verified: two detected full-range 2 MiB reads match, separate verification passes, and the factory application returns from ROM. Inspect PCB, FPGA and oscillator markings and attached header wiring next. Then evaluate the documented CPU-less SPIBone identifier/scratch route before synthetic transport tests.</p><p>For the PCI card, confirm markings, JTAG adapter voltage support and GND/VREF measurements. A read-only scan and cold-cycle recovery path precede programming. These remain physical gates.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">SOURCE REVISIONS / NOT OUR BOARD PERFORMANCE</p><h2>Keep the designs tied to the evidence.</h2></div></div><div class="source-list"><article class="source-card"><h2>Adiuvo schematic</h2><p>Reviewed drawing dated {sources.forgix_schematic.drawing_date}; drawing revision blank. PSRAM belongs to RP QSPI.</p><a href={sources.forgix_schematic.url}>Open pinned primary schematic ↗</a><p class="revision">{sources.forgix_schematic.repository_revision}</p></article>{sources.repositories.filter(item => item.repo!=="ESPARGOS/esp-sdr").map(item => <article class="source-card"><h2>{item.repo}</h2><a href={`https://github.com/${item.repo}/tree/${item.revision}`}>Open pinned primary source ↗</a><p class="revision">{item.revision}</p></article>)}</div><p class="calc-note">Full review and references: <a href={evidenceUrl("docs/evidence/fpga-inventory/source-revisions.json")}>source metadata</a>, <a href="https://www.efinixinc.com/docs/trion8-ds-v5.5.pdf">T8 package/memory datasheet</a>, <a href="https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/rp2350/rp2350-datasheet.pdf">RP full-speed USB specification</a>. No FPGA transport or integrated RF performance is accepted.</p></section>
</Base>
